{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795256425,"nonce":"NXntUca0TNjvxZdOkNTLiRp+axc=","title":"A bound subtree with an SVG keeps its groups static, so moving it repaints the whole tree","message":"`paint/motion.rs` turns `moving_groups_dynamic` off for a bound subtree that `subtree_has_media` (an image or an SVG below it), so its shared groups are retained in the static batch. Rows then decline every frame it moves (`rows_unavailable reason=moving_static_binding`) and the frame is a full paint.\n\nWhere it costs: cn_demo's first calendar (\"Meetings, weather and a deadline\") marks days with SVG icons. A page or grid holding one is a static binding. Over 12 continuous month turns in `cn_demo_costs` (`COSTS_CALENDAR=12 COSTS_CALENDAR_PHASE=turn COSTS_CALENDAR_FRAMES=12 COSTS_CALENDAR_DT=8 COSTS_ASYNC=1`, without `COSTS_NO_TRACE`), 26 of 144 frames are full for this reason, against 23 for the structural frames of the turns and 95 on rows.\n\nTried: limiting the rule to images (`ElementType::Image` only), so an SVG page's groups go dynamic. The rows frame and the full paint of the same pose then agree, but both are wrong: the leaving November grid, which is translated out of the clipped `.cn-calendar-months` and fading, is drawn at its untranslated place inside the clip (`COSTS_CALENDAR_SNAP=\u003cprefix\u003e`, compare `\u003cprefix\u003e-turn-full.png` before and after). So an SVG inside a dynamic group does not take the group's transform or clip yet; captured SVG ordinals (932902d) are not enough on their own.\n\nWanted: an SVG under a moving group placed and clipped by the group on rows, then drop SVG from the rule.","files":null}]}